<Base title="Our activities — DET.io Foundation" description="How DET.io Foundation puts its public-benefit mission into practice through open education, software development, and privacy and AI safety research." path="/activities" pageType="CollectionPage" breadcrumbs={[{name:"Home",href:"/"},{name:"Our activities",href:"/activities"}]}>
<div class="container-site"><div class="editorial-hero"><p class="folio">OUR ACTIVITIES / REVIEWED 17 SEPTEMBER 2026</p><h1>Research people can read.<br/>Technology they can examine.</h1><p class="intro">We advance education, digital rights, infrastructure resilience, and technology safety by publishing knowledge and developing open systems. Our current work serves learners, researchers, developers, and infrastructure operators.</p></div>
<nav class="path-tabs" aria-label="Activities on this page"><a href="#education">Open education</a><a href="#software">Software development</a><a href="#safety">Privacy &amp; safety</a><a href="#progress">Progress &amp; availability</a></nav>
<section class="editorial-section" id="education"><p class="folio">01 / OPEN EDUCATION</p><div><h2>Make the underlying ideas accessible.</h2><p>Cloud computing, identity verification, and multi-agent AI affect people who may never inspect the systems themselves. We publish explanations that connect a technical design to the problem it is intended to address, alongside references that let readers go deeper.</p><p>The VirtEngine learning library follows a computing agreement from a resource request through bidding, leasing, usage, and payment. Its module reference and technical documentation connect that explanation to the implementation. On this site, research topics describe questions about privacy, confidential computing, incentives, and AI oversight.</p><p>These materials support students, independent learners, and researchers. Reading them does not require payment, a protocol token, Foundation membership, or an identity check. They are resources for self-directed learning, rather than accredited courses.</p><div class="foundation-actions"><a class="foundation-button" href="https://virtengine.com/learn">Explore the learning library ↗</a><a class="foundation-link" href="/research">Follow a research question →</a></div></div></section>
<section class="editorial-section" id="software"><p class="folio">02 / OPEN DEVELOPMENT</p><div><h2>Publish the implementation for scrutiny.</h2><p>VirtEngine develops an open cloud marketplace protocol: the rules for resource orders, provider bids, leases, identity, and settlement. Publishing the code lets developers examine how those rules are represented and identify where the implementation needs improvement.</p><p>Bosun is an experimental open-source orchestrator for AI coding agents. It provides an applied setting for exploring task coordination, review gates, and recovery while people retain oversight. Developers can study the source, report reproducible problems, and propose improvements to code or documentation.</p><p>The intended public benefit is reusable, inspectable technology and knowledge. Open source makes scrutiny possible; it does not by itself establish production reliability, independent security assurance, or achieved social impact.</p><div class="foundation-actions"><a class="foundation-button" href="/research/virtengine">Explore VirtEngine →</a><a class="foundation-link" href="/research/bosun">Explore Bosun →</a><a class="foundation-link" href="/participate#contribute">Find a contribution →</a></div></div></section>
<section class="editorial-section" id="safety"><p class="folio">03 / PRIVACY &amp; SAFETY</p><div><h2>Ask how systems remain accountable.</h2><p>Our identity work examines how verification can limit disclosure of sensitive information. VEID explores encrypted inputs, verification by network participants, and proofs that services could use without receiving the full underlying identity record. Important questions include consent, access, recovery, and the risk of linking people across contexts.</p><p>DSEMA explores how multi-agent AI could adapt under verifiable controls. Its research considers audit records, constraints on execution, human oversight, and the governance of changes to the system itself. Bosun provides a separate, experimental engineering context for some of those coordination and review questions.</p><p>These published designs give researchers and developers concrete proposals to examine. They describe research aims and proposed controls, not proven guarantees that a system is safe or a claim of regulatory accreditation.</p><div class="foundation-actions"><a class="foundation-button" href="/research/privacy-preserving-verification">Explore privacy research →</a><a class="foundation-link" href="/research/multi-agent-safety">Explore AI safety research →</a></div></div></section>
<section class="editorial-section" id="progress"><p class="folio">04 / PROGRESS &amp; AVAILABILITY</p><div><h2>Separate present outputs from future goals.</h2><p>Our public outputs include source repositories, technical documentation, learning guides, research explanations, and this Foundation’s governance and constitution explorer. Those are the materials visitors can read and examine today.</p><p><strong>VirtEngine:</strong> the network remains in development. TestNet is planned for January 2027 and MainNet for March 2027, subject to testing and separate approval. Check <a href="https://virtengine.com/network">official network status</a> before planning participation.</p><p><strong>DSEMA:</strong> a research architecture for accountable multi-agent systems. <strong>Bosun:</strong> experimental software available for inspection and contribution. <strong>Identity &amp; VEID:</strong> identity protocol research and reference work; the Foundation does not operate a central VEID verification service.</p><p>Greater access, better privacy, and more accountable infrastructure are intended benefits. We do not present them as measured outcomes of deployed programs. Published annual reports and audited financial statements are not currently available on this site; our <a href="/transparency">transparency page</a> records reporting status, available documents, and funding disclosures.</p><div class="editorial-status"><p><strong>DETIO FOUNDATION LTD</strong> is an Australian not-for-profit public company limited by guarantee, ACN 699 651 771. Its constitutional charitable purposes are distinct from ACNC registration, which this site does not claim.</p></div><div class="foundation-actions"><a class="foundation-button" href="/participate">Find your next step →</a><a class="foundation-link" href="/contact">Ask about our work →</a></div></div></section></div>
